Christian Bale says portraying Oakland Raiders owner Al Davis in &#x201C; Madden &#x201D; is one of his favorite roles from his four-decade career. That's extremely high praise considering Bale's resume is longer than a CVS receipt, and includes winning an Oscar (for &#x201C;The Fighter&#x201D;) and playing Batman three times.

So why did Bale enjoy playing the eccentric football team owner so much?

&#x201C;He had so many just wonderful contradictions,&#x201D; Bale told Variety at the Amazon MGM Studios film's world premiere earlier this month. &#x201C;He was such a strong character. He liked to intimidate people, you know; he said all this 'Just win, baby' and 'Dominate.' It's a game of psychological intimidation and fear.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Rajinikanth’s 'Jailer 2' Sets Global Streaming Premiere Date on Prime Video Amazon CEO Says Prime Video Is Profitable and Generates 'Tens of Billions of Dollars' Annually; Content Spending Grew 7% in Q3 to $5.9 Billion

On the flip side, Davis had &#x201C;one of the biggest hearts of anybody,&#x201D; Bale said. &#x201C;He took care of people. He kept this very quiet. He didn't really like people knowing about how much he cared for others.&#x201D; In truth, Davis, who owned the NFL team for 39 years, from 1972 until his death in 2011, lived the mantra of &#x201C;Once a Raider, Always a Raider.&#x201D; Bale explained: &#x201C;He kept caring for [players] after they were long gone from the roster. But he was just an icon. He was a trailblazer, and he seemed to know what he wanted to do in life from a very, very early age and did it. It's quite incredible and very, very unique.&#x201D;

In &#x201C;Madden,&#x201D; now playing in theaters and streaming on Prime Video, director David O. Russell explores the special bond between Davis and the Raiders' Super Bowl-winning coach John Madden (Nicolas Cage). The film follows as their relationship evolves from owner and coach to a deeper, though sometimes complicated, friendship when Madden retires from coaching and starts a career in the broadcast booth. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Since Bale and Cage are both famous for diving deep into their characters, O. Russell encouraged them to riff on set. One of their ad-libs made the trailer, with Bale's Davis introducing Cage's Madden to a hot new rap group &#x2014; N.W.A.

&#x201C;I'm used to working with David, and I love it,&#x201D; Bale said. (&#x201C;Madden&#x201D; marks the actor and director's fourth collaboration, following 2010's &#x201C;The Fighter,&#x201D; 2013's &#x201C;American Hustle&#x201D; and 2022's &#x201C;Amsterdam.&#x201D;) &#x201C;David writes beautiful scripts, so we obviously do that. But then he's often shouting new lines out at us. He loves it when we start going off script as well, and so it creates a real atmosphere of fun and creativity, and it ends up looking incredible, having been imbued with life.&#x201D;

Aside from the focus on football, &#x201C;Madden&#x201D; also spotlights Al Davis' love story with his wife Carol Davis, portrayed in the film by Sienna Miller.

&#x201C;What was so moving was their absolute devotion to each other,&#x201D; said Miller. &#x201C;Al lived and breathed football. That was No. 1. The only thing that would keep him away from a game was his love for his wife.&#x201D;

That devotion was epitomized when Carol suffered a stroke in 1979. "[Al] stayed by her bed. He slept in the hospital. He did not leave her side. I guess you'd hope that was the case, but the world stopped for him,&#x201D; Miller said. &#x201C;It was that love that I wanted to bring into the film.&#x201D; [Carol Davis recovered and, after inheriting ownership of the team from Al, led the Raiders until her death in 2025.]

As much passion as the Davises had for each other, they also had a passion for fashion. &#x201C;Madden&#x201D; includes a goofy montage where Al and Carol try on a myriad of snazzy '80s getups, but the sequence doubles as a genuinely sweet tribute to their love. Did Bale take any of Davis' jackets or his signature pinky ring home from set?

&#x201C;I didn't take any of the jackets, but I did take Super Bowl ring,&#x201D; Bale admitted. &#x201C;That's in a very nice little box on a shelf.&#x201D;

After Davis, Bale is soon set to take on another legend &#x2014; playing Lt. Vincent Hanna in Michael Mann's long-awaited &#x201C; Heat 2 .&#x201D;

&#x201C;I was very reticent because I thought, 'Oh, these are legends. These are icons. Like, how can you compete with that?'&#x201D; Bale said about taking on a role originated by Al Pacino. &#x201C;Talking with Michael, well, he's written an absolutely brilliant script. He's a phenomenal director, and I thought, 'All right, I'm a coward if I don't try doing this.' So, I'm enjoying figuring out how to play that one.&#x201D;

As Netflix 's The Body surpasses 5M views in its first week, a petition to remove the show from the platform is also growing in numbers.

Criticizing the "blasphemous anti-Christian series" from creator Quinn Shepard ahead of its release last week, the CitizenGo petition has accumulated more than 126K signatures calling on Netflix to "stop defiling the faith of millions of Christian families and cancel The Body before it reaches our living rooms." Deadline has reached out to Netflix.

"Once the show reaches your living room and your teenager's phone, the damage is done. Nobody can take it back," reads the petition addressed to Netflix's Chief Content Officer Peter Rice. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

It seems the alleged damage might already have been inflicted, with Netflix reporting that the coming-of-age horror series received 5.1M views in its first five days, landing at No. 3 on the streamer's Global Top 10 English TV list, in addition to ranking in the Top 10 in 80 countries. Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

The petition takes issue with the depiction of "Christian schoolgirls, a dark initiation ritual, the Devil and 'prophetic visions'" in the show's trailer .

"This is a pattern. First Netflix mocked Jesus Christ Himself in The First Temptation of Christ . Then it sexualized eleven-year-old girls in Cuties . Now it has come for Christian schoolgirls," it reads. "Each time, Netflix pushes one step further into the family home.

"Ask yourself this. Would Netflix ever turn Muslim prayer, Hindu worship or even Wiccan ritual into a sex-and-Satan horror story for teenagers? Of course not. Netflix does this to Christians because it believes we will stay quiet and keep paying. It is time to prove Netflix wrong. A few complaints get ignored. But when Christians of every church stand together, Netflix feels it in its subscriber count," the petition adds.

Shephard, whose grandmother was an Evangelical minister, previously told Deadline, "We weren't trying to make a show that was hyper-critical of religion . Obviously, religion is a theme in the show, and it touches on it in a lot of ways." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

In The Body , all eight episodes now available to stream on Netflix, a group of badly-behaved Catholic school girls begin having prophetic visions that set off mass hysteria in town after a dance-team initiation goes wrong on Halloween night in 2004.

&#x201C; Glee &#x201D; co-creator Ian Brennan admits he wasn&#x2019;t always open to the upcoming &#x201C;Glee&#x201D; reboot.

&#x201C;I wasn&#x2019;t that excited about it,&#x201D; he told me earlier this week at an FYC event for his latest television project &#x201C; Monster: The Lizzie Borden Story .&#x201D; &#x201C;Every time it came up, it was like, &#x2018;Why would you do that again?&#x2019; For whatever reason, in the last six months or so, I completely did a 180 about it. It just seems the idea is right. I think the time is right. Now I&#x2019;m really excited about it. It&#x2019;s going to be a lot of fun.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories First Lady Melania Trump to Participate in Fox News' Annual Christmas Tree Lighting Fox News Sets Midterm Elections Coverage: Here's How to Stream 'Democracy 26' Online Free

In September, creator Ryan Murphy revealed he had just completed the first script for a reboot. &#x201C;Brad [Falchuk], Ian and I, who wrote all the first two seasons, have written something,&#x201D; he told Entertainment Tonight. &#x201C;I&#x2019;ve been in touch with around 10 of the original cast members. It&#x2019;s very sweet, and they all had a lot of questions, but they all were very enthusiastic about the idea.&#x201D;

Brennan told me, &#x201C;You&#x2019;re catching these characters at a totally different part of their life &#x2026; The timing of these characters thinking, &#x2018;Maybe that was the best time in my life, being in that choir in high school&#x2019; and then once you think that you&#x2019;re like, &#x2018;Oh, that show&#x2019;s going to work.&#x2019;&#x201D;

While a production start date has yet to be set, Brennan touched on how the reboot may handle the deaths of Finn actor Cory Monteith, who suffered a fatal accidental heroin overdose, and Naya Rivera, who played Santana and died after she drowned in 2020 while trying to save her four-year-old son during a boat outing. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;We&#x2019;re still figuring a lot of it out,&#x201D; Brennan said. &#x201C;That&#x2019;s going to be part of it, that sadness and that loss. But still in all, I think ["Glee"] is too big of a thing to sort of let lay. There&#x2019;s something about that feels right right now.&#x201D;

As for Brennan&#x2019;s song picks for the reboot, he said, &#x201C;We didn&#x2019;t do enough Journey. We did almost all of Journey but there&#x2019;s still a bunch of hits.&#x201D;

The &#x201C;Monster&#x201D; anthology is a far cry (or scream, for that matter) from &#x201C;Glee.&#x201D; I know ["Monster"] is a much different animal, but actually at its core like all writing it&#x2019;s trying to get inside the head of someone else's mind,&#x201D; Brennan said. &#x201C;I&#x2019;m stunned at how fun it is to do this show.&#x201D;

Before Murphy suggested Lizzie Borden to his team they were working on three different seasons around Luigi Mangione, the 1984 New York City subway shooter Bernie Goetz and the Unabomber. &#x201C;I don't think it's talking out of turn because we're never going to do it,&#x201D; Brennan said. &#x201C;We were going to do like a triptych of Luigi Mangione, Bernie Goetz and Unabomber. It was really interesting about male rage, about vigilantes. And it was just hard to write. It was like pushing like a dead mule up a hill. Luigi, we don't know anything about. Bernie Goetz is sort of interesting a bit in that sort of Michael Douglas in &#x201C;Falling Down&#x201D; kind of way. Kaczynski is fascinating, very bright, a very strange mind, but nothing really sexy about that story really.&#x201D;

Ella Beatty stars in the show as the titular Lizzie Borden. She often returned home after a day of shooting covered in fake blood. &#x201C;Shaving cream actually is a great hack to get fake blood off of your skin and out of your hair,&#x201D; Beatty said, adding, &#x201C;I feel like I was always covered in blood. I feel like I almost never wasn&#x2019;t.&#x201D;

She joked that she &#x201C;frequently&#x201D; took &#x201C;shaving cream baths.&#x201D;

Charlie Hunnam , who plays Lizzie&#x2019;s father, said his love of axes began way before he signed on for the show. He actually has a collection of about a dozen axes. &#x201C;Some of them are in my garage, some of them are in my pickup truck,&#x201D; he said. &#x201C;I have like a sick obsession. I cannot drive past a wood pile in L.A. or anywhere when a tree has been felled and they leave all of those rounds of wood on the road I have to like a complete crazy person pull over and fill my pickup truck with wood and then go cut it. I have a little back area in my office building, and I probably have three, four or five tons of chopped firewood.&#x201D;

Magnolia Pictures has snatched up North American rights to "Trash Mountain," a dramedy film starring Caleb Hearon , who co-wrote the script with Ruby Caster, and Zooey Deschanel . A theatrical release is in the works for next year.

"I Used to Go Here" filmmaker Kris Rey directs "Trash Mountain," and Colin Trevorrow serves as producer. The movie held its premiere at the Toronto International Film Festival in September. Related Stories Versant CEO: MS NOW Not Suffering From 'News Fatigue' Like Fox News Did Midterm Elections Cause Changes in News World Order?

According to an official logline, "'Trash Mountain' follows the story of Gavin (Hearon), a young gay Chicago man who is forced to return to his hometown in rural Missouri following the death of his hoarder father. The story takes us on a journey of emotional acceptance and resilience as Gavin and his half-sister Abbi (Deschanel) navigate challenging family dynamics and their complicated relationships with the past." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Other cast members include Jacki Weaver, Jaboukie Young-White, Kyle Marvin and Holmes.

&#x201C;'Trash Mountain' is such a funny, smart, joyful work, which is no surprise coming from the brilliant mind of Caleb Hearon,&#x201D; said Magnolia Pictures co-CEOs Eamonn Bowles and Dori Begley. &#x201C;We're so excited to collaborate with Caleb, Kris, Colin and this fantastic cast to bring it to audiences.&#x201D;

Metronome Film Company presents, in association with Sight Unseen, Pigasus Pictures, Five Sticks Productions and Streeterville Productions. Rebecca Linfoot co-produced "Trash Mountain." Executive producers include Zachary Spicer, Julia Lebedev, Eddie Vaisman, Hearon, Lilly Wachowski, Annys Hamilton, Carrie Holt De Lama, Kelley Sims, Chris Cafero, Scott L. Goldstein, George Rush and Willie Trieger. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;'Trash Mountain' is a film about home. The physical homes we reside in, the emotions that we make home in, the place where we grew up, and the way that many of us make home elsewhere when we've spilled out over the brims of our hometowns,&#x201D; said Hearon. &#x201C;I've been a fan of Magnolia films for a very long time and we're honored to be partnering with them.&#x201D;

Hearon, a 31-year-old stand-up comedian and host of the "So True with Caleb Hearon" podcast, has seen his star rise in recent years, landing memorable supporting roles in films like "Pizza Movie," "The Devil Wears Prada 2" and "Little Brother." His other film credits include "Jurassic World: Dominion," "I Used to Be Funny" and "Sweethearts." Deschanel, best known for her turn as Jess in the long-running Fox sitcom "New Girl," was last seen in the Prime Video holiday rom-com "Merv" with Charlie Cox. Her other recent big-screen credits include "Harold and the Purple Crayon" and "Trolls Band Together."

The deal was negotiated by Magnolia Pictures SVP of Acquisitions John Von Thaden and VP of Acquisitions Miranda Hill, and by CAA Media Finance and WME on behalf of the filmmakers.

Veteran industry exec Tendo Nagenda is joining Proximity Media , as its new President. In this role, Nagenda will oversee all aspects of creative development and production across the company&#x2019;s film, television and nonfiction divisions, reporting directly to the founders, to advance Proximity&#x2019;s creative strategy and deliver their slate of projects. Nagenda will assume the role on November 30th.

&#x201C;Tendo has spent his career working alongside talented filmmakers, championing original ideas and helping make projects that resonate with audiences around the world,&#x201D; said Proximity co-founders Ryan Coogler , Zinzi Coogler and Sev Ohanian, Founders of Proximity Media, in a joint statement. &#x201C;As Proximity continues to grow across film, television and nonfiction, we&#x2019;re excited to have his creative instincts and experience helping guide this next chapter. He shares our belief in the power of storytelling to connect people, challenge perspectives and create meaningful impact, and we&#x2019;re thrilled to welcome him to the team.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News Ryan Coogler's 'The X-Files' Reboot Picked Up To Series At Hulu News 'Black Panther' Actor Winston Duke Reveals What He Told David Jonsson About Taking On The Iconic Role

As President, he will oversee Proximity&#x2019;s creative divisions, guiding projects from ideation through production while helping shape the company&#x2019;s broader creative and business strategy. The heads of Film, Television and Nonfiction will report directly to Nagenda, who will work alongside Terra Potts, who oversees Marketing, Operations and the In Proximity podcast, and Proximity Co-Founder Ludwig G&#xF6;ransson, who oversees Music. Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

&#x201C;I&#x2019;m honored and excited to join Ryan, Zinzi, Sev and the entire Proximity team,&#x201D; said Nagenda. &#x201C;Their commitment to ambitious, meaningful storytelling reflects everything I&#x2019;ve always believed in, and I look forward to building on what they&#x2019;ve created, collaborating with extraordinary filmmakers and creators, and bringing compelling new stories to audiences around the world.&#x201D;

Nagenda previously served as Vice President of Original Film at Netflix, where he helped build the streamer&#x2019;s original film slate and oversaw a range of acclaimed projects, including Spike Lee&#x2019;s Da 5 Bloods , The Old Guard , Ma Rainey&#x2019;s Black Bottom , The Harder They Fall and Glass Onion: A Knives Out Mystery . Prior to Netflix, he served as Executive Vice President of Production at Walt Disney Studios, overseeing films across the studio&#x2019;s live-action slate, including Beauty and the Beast , Cinderella , Saving Mr. Banks , Mulan , A Wrinkle in Time and Queen of Katwe . blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

In 2022, Nagenda founded 10 by Ten Entertainment, a production company focused on developing and producing original stories from distinctive and underrepresented perspectives. His first produced feature, The Book of Clarence , written and directed by Jeymes Samuel, was released theatrically by Sony Pictures in January 2024.

The appointment comes as Proximity Media continues to expand its slate across film, television and nonfiction. The company is behind the critically acclaimed blockbuster Sinners , which grossed more than $365 million worldwide, as well as Creed III and Academy Award-winning Judas and the Black Messiah . On the television side, Proximity recently secured a series greenlight for its highly anticipated reimagining of The X-Files for Hulu, Danielle Deadwyler and Himesh Patel attached to star. The company also recently entered into a multiyear television deal with Netflix to develop an exclusive slate of scripted and unscripted projects. Its nonfiction projects include National Geographic&#x2019;s Hurricane Katrina: Race Against Time , which became the network&#x2019;s most-watched U.S. streaming title, along with Stephen Curry: Underrated , Homeroom and Anthem .

&#x201C; Grand Theft Auto VI&#x201D; is poised to break sales records , and could even shift the economy today as scores of fans took the day off of work to cause digital mayhem. But some right-wing pundits aren't thrilled with all of the attention the video game is getting.

Fox News had a roundtable discussion on the Nov. 19 episode of &#x201C;Outnumbered&#x201D; about the game and adults who take the day off to play it, and clips of the discussion posted on X by journalist Acyn Torabi have gained attention. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Chris Pratt to Continue 'Terminal List' Story in 'Savage Son' Series for Amazon Chris Pratt to Star in Sci-Fi Family Drama 'The Traveler,' Inks First-Look Producing Deal at Paramount (EXCLUSIVE)

&#x201C;Outnumbered&#x201D; co-host Harris Faulkner criticized fans taking paid time off as shirking their civic duties, saying, &#x201C;If this generation wants to preach about affordability, but they're willing to cost billions of dollars in revenue loss on a day like today to go play 'GTA6,' that probably tells you everything you need to know &#x2026; Get yourself to work.&#x201D;

Fox News contributor Paul Mauro agreed, saying, &#x201C;You're taking day off of work, you're abdicating your responsibilities to whoever it is in your life so you can do this nonsense? I mean, c'mon, grow up.&#x201D;

Mauro was also upset with the game's violence and how he thinks it could impact kids, saying, &#x201C;This is almost the equivalent of giving a kid a gun at an age when they don&#x2019;t understand the responsibility.&#x201D;

Meanwhile, Manosphere influencers are frustrated that the game encourages players to treat main character Jason's girlfriend, Lucia, with respect.

Clavicular took to X on Nov. 18 to write, &#x201C;&#x2018;GTA 6&#x2019; is insanely cucked, half of the missions are jestermaxing and simping for girls.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Myron Gaines wrote on X on Nov. 19, &#x201C;Despite the game getting solid first day reviews, this is yet another example of how political correctness, inclusivity and feminism has destroyed a legendary game series &#x2026; The main character gets cucked by his gf the whole time &#x2026;&#x201D;

Zack Hoyt, better known online as Asmongold, complained during a stream of the game that, &#x201C;I had to watch a stupid TV show with her, rub her feet and listen to her friends&#x2019; stories about Snapchat &#x2026; Do I have go to the corner store and buy her some tampons too?&#x201D;

Despite chatter from commentators, &#x201C;GTA 6&#8243; is breaking internet usage records and is already one of the best-reviewed games of all time.
